> *** Comments: Please present your comments for this paper

This paper studied Subgraph-representation Based Method applied in Email Sp=
oofing Detection. In order to solve some problems that the traditional emai=
l content-based detectors are ineffective, this paper constructed an Asset =
Co-occurence Graph and introduced an enffective detection based on subgraph=
-representation learning. The empirical results look very promising.
However, there are still some concerns that need to be addressed.
1.	Some sentences contain grammatical mistakes. For example, in the abstrac=
t, =E2=80=9CFinally, the experimental results evaluate on two public datase=
ts, Nazario and DataCon, show that=E2=80=9D lacks a conjunction. The author=
 should revise the whole paper carefully.
2.	In figure 6, you should mark what the horizontal and vertical coordinate=
s mean.
3.	There are few experiments. You should compare more SOTA methods on more =
and larger datasets.
4.	About randomly splitting the datasets, I suggest that the training and t=
est datasets are as independent as possible to test the ability of the prop=
osed method to deal with new mail frauds.
5.	Email content is also an important part of email Spoofing detection. It =
might be better to take the content of the email into account.

> *** Overall Recommendation: What is your overall recommendation of this p=
aper?
Minor (3)

