> *** Comments: Please present your comments for this paper

This article studies a series of methods for detecting E-mail spoofing, as =
well as anti-spoofing solutions. It proposes SpoofingGuard, an email spoofi=
ng framework based on ACGraph. It uses graph representation learning and su=
pervised learning to prevent emails from spoofing attacks, which solves the=
 problem of low efficiency of traditional content-based email detection. Sp=
oofingguard achieves excellent results in email spoofing detection in publi=
c data sets in the experimental section. It has more powerful detection and=
 recognition ability in the face of complex email content.=20
Some comments:
1=EF=BC=89The background of mail fraud is not sufficiently introduced in th=
e introduction.
2=EF=BC=89In C of Part III, the description of Figure 5 is too brief for re=
aders to fully understand.
3=EF=BC=89In the experimental results section of IV, the series introductio=
n of experimental results is not sufficient.
4=EF=BC=89In Section V, it is necessary to describe in detail the reasons w=
hy a new email is judged to be a legitimate email when its structure is sim=
ilar to that of a legitimate email
5=EF=BC=89The summary at the end of Part VII is not sufficient.

